{"id": "EUVD-2026-80577", "enisaUuid": "8f30ea93-5d04-3e60-a431-b7962a376bbc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ethosu: check MMIO mapping errors in probe\n\ndevm_platform_ioremap_resource() returns an error pointer when the register\nresource cannot be mapped. ethosu_probe() stores it and continues until\ninitialization dereferences it through MMIO accessors.\n\nReturn the mapping error before initializing the device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7aad73b481194e3f0efba9688e9a5914bbd036b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ab64476a610fe65858fdc37c7a30caa13e334ac"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89977", "GHSA-c8v6-r4v4-jmq9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2b200abf-ebc4-34a9-8683-b4864f4fba0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "535b63d8-6cd7-3c23-ba99-4c2f57b987f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5bcbfdb5-9c31-382d-aca6-c631de842518", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a5e9c0228e613f0ef2a58b9782d7c0ea8f1e58b <7ab64476a610fe65858fdc37c7a30caa13e334ac"}, {"id": "799a6a31-13ba-315e-9b7f-96e8d06da390", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bb19a036-e3a8-3033-b93d-7b164e58f5b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "d5a74d17-f951-3896-91c0-e6c0bb168851", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a5e9c0228e613f0ef2a58b9782d7c0ea8f1e58b <f7aad73b481194e3f0efba9688e9a5914bbd036b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ffcc92ef-d752-3725-a5f4-bb2fb791f517", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}